## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical guardrails for real-world, globally distributed Azure workloads, focusing on logs/telemetry leakage, secret rotation, and safe rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Managed Identities with least privilege RBAC
- Key Vault references over inline secrets
- Azure Policy gates (no secrets in env vars/connection strings)
- Application Insights masking and diagnostic redaction
- Canary deployments with telemetry-driven rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js example: fetch secret via DefaultAzureCredential and KeyVaultSecretClient
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { SecretClient } = require('@azure/keyvault-secrets');
const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const client = new SecretClient("https://<kv-name>.vault.azure.net/", credential);
async function getSecret(name) {
  const secret = await client.getSecret(name);
  return secret.value;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the guardrail during a canary rollout?
- What logging changes would you implement to ensure no secrets are emitted even in error traces?

## Why This Is Asked
This question validates the ability to design an automated security response system for multi-tenant Azure SaaS environments, integrating threat detection with immediate containment and recovery capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Anomaly detection using Defender for Cloud analytics and Sentinel ML models
- Event Grid-based alert routing and per-tenant processing
- Automated resource isolation via NSG rules, private endpoint restrictions, and conditional access policies
- Key Vault credential rotation and token revocation workflows
- Deployment slot rollback with feature flag coordination
- Comprehensive audit trails across all security actions

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-logic for automated breach response
async function handleSecurityAlert(alert) {
  if (alert.severity > 3) {
    await isolateTenantResources(alert.tenantId);
    await rotateCompromisedCredentials(alert.tenantId);
    await initiateSafeRollback(alert.tenantId);
  }
}
```

